{
    "background_story": "Willa was a brilliant geologist who spent her career studying the world's most fascinating river systems. Her life's work was centered around the concept of confluence - the meeting of two or more bodies of water. She became particularly obsessed with the confluence of the Colorado and Green rivers in Canyonlands National Park. Willa's research led her to develop groundbreaking theories on the geological and ecological significance of these merged waterways. Her work took her to the most remote and breathtaking locations on earth, from the Amazon to the Mekong. As she explored the confluences of the world's rivers, Willa discovered that the concept also applied to her own life - the merging of her passions, her relationships, and her sense of purpose. Her journey became a metaphor for the beauty and power of confluence.",
